  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 531 AM EDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nInto mid-week the ridge begins to push back to the west and break \ndown a tad pushing our area into a more dry pattern Wednesday \nthrough Friday. With the drier air in place, dewpoints will be quite \npleasant in the low 60s across the area by Friday afternoon.Temps \nwill also top out in the upper 80s to low 90s across the area. \nPushing into the weekend a trough swings down into the TN/KY area \nwhich will in turn push in a frontal boundary during this time period \nwhich increases rain chances Saturday through Monday. Too early to \ndetermine a severe risk if any but will be keeping an eye on this \nsystem as it tracks into our area. Temperatures will continue to be \npleasant into the weekend with highs most days in the mid to upper \n80s.",
